<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 74,662 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 74,662 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 74,662 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 44,651 tonnes on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			16,013	    15,932</p>
<p>    Import cargo			58,649	    28,719</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven ships are expected to sail and seven to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to</p>
<p>unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>High speed diesel   78,750	 Chesa Peak City    27/3</p>
<p>General cargo	 5,428	  Hang Man	     27/3</p>
<p>Palm oil		8,200	  Global Juno	  28/3</p>
<p>Furnace oil	   42,000	 Athenian Pride     28/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
